---
description: Never use em dashes in user-facing copy or generated text
alwaysApply: true
---

# No em dashes

Never use em dashes (—), or a spaced hyphen standing in for one, in UI copy, error messages, placeholders, tooltips, or any other user-facing text. Rewrite with a period, comma, or colon instead.

```
❌ "Session expired — sign back in to resume syncing."
✅ "Session expired. Sign back in to resume syncing."

❌ "Optional — shown in the menu"
✅ "Optional, shown in the menu"
```

The bare "—" glyph used as an empty-value placeholder in tables and stats is allowed.
